This project contains three kinds of material, under three different terms.
Read the part that applies to what you want to use.


================================================================================
1. THE TEXT OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA
================================================================================

Files:  constitution/source/*
        constitution/site/data/constitution.js
        constitution/site/data/schedules.js
        constitution/site/data/amendments.js
        the "official text" sections of the website

This is Government of India material. It is not mine to license, and no claim is
made over it.

Source
    The Constitution of India, as on 1st May 2024
    Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India
    Updated to the Constitution (One Hundred and Sixth Amendment) Act, 2023
    https://cdnbbsr.s3waas.gov.in/s380537a945c7aaa788ccfcdf1b99b5d8f/uploads/2024/07/20240716890312078.pdf

It is reproduced here on two footings.

    Section 52(1)(q)(ii) of the Copyright Act, 1957 provides that reproducing or
    publishing an Act of a legislature is not an infringement of copyright, on
    the condition that it is reproduced or published "together with any
    commentary thereon or any other original matter". This project is
    commentary-first: every article carries a plain-language reading, and much
    of it carries judgment summaries, examination notes and diagrams besides.

    The Government of India's standard website reproduction terms permit
    material to be reproduced free of charge, provided it is reproduced
    accurately, is not used in a derogatory manner or in a misleading context,
    and the source is prominently acknowledged. The text here is reproduced
    verbatim, including its footnote markers and its markings for omitted words;
    the source is named on the overview page, on the About page, and in the
    footer of every page of the site.

If you reuse the text, those same conditions apply to you. They come from the
statute and the government's terms, not from this project, and nothing here can
widen or narrow them.


================================================================================
2. THE COMMENTARY WRITTEN FOR THIS PROJECT
================================================================================

Files:  constitution/site/data/explain-*.js     plain-language readings
        constitution/site/data/cases-*.js       landmark judgment summaries
        constitution/site/data/exam-*.js        examination notes
        constitution/site/data/maps.js          diagrams
        constitution/site/data/amendmeta.js     amendment descriptions
        constitution/build/FACTCHECK.md         the audit record
        constitution/README.md

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(CC BY 4.0).

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt this material, including commercially, provided you give
appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate if changes were made.

Two things worth saying plainly, since this material concerns law:

    It is commentary, not law, and not legal advice. Where it describes a
    judgment it is paraphrasing, not quoting.

    It has been audited but it is not certified correct. The record of that
    audit, including 48 corrections and an honest account of what the audit does
    not establish, is in constitution/build/FACTCHECK.md. If you republish this
    material, do not represent it as more reliable than that record supports.


